// ROADMAP.md additions
// ============================================================================
//
// Add under ## v0.5 — Internal Architecture:
//
// ### Indel equivalence expansion — known limitations
//
// **MNP / complex allele expansion deferred.**
// Multi-nucleotide polymorphisms where both REF and ALT are > 1 bp cannot
// be slid through repeat context because the sliding condition breaks down.
// These are stored as-is with a tracing::warn.  A future implementation
// could left-align complex alleles using the `vt decompose` / `bcftools norm
// --atomize` approach before expansion.
//
// **BED padding is position-based, not sequence-based.**
// `with_indel_padding(n)` extends every BED interval by n bp on each side
// without inspecting the reference sequence.  This may include false-positive
// masking of bases outside the actual repeat.  A sequence-aware version would
// identify the repeat boundary from the FASTA and expand only to that boundary.
//
// **Store scan-back constant MAX_SCAN_BACK = 256.**
// `overlapping_multi` scans back at most 256 entries from the binary-search
// upper bound to find large deletions that start before query_start but still
// overlap.  Deletions > 256 bp (rare in SNP/indel VCFs; common in SV VCFs)
// may be missed.  Replace with a proper interval-tree (e.g., `bio::data_structures::
// interval_tree`) when SV support is added.
//
// **Strand-aware diagnostic overlap not implemented.**
// SegregateVariants::overlaps() accepts `is_reverse` but ignores it.
// VCF records carry no strand information; if a future workflow creates
// strand-specific diagnostic VCFs, extend DiagnosticSite with an
// optional `Strand` field and filter in overlaps().
